      "parameters": {
        "description": "=Use this tool as the first validation step to check the entire workflow carefully before execution. It must not modify data or send anything — only validate and log results.\n\nValidation order:\n\n1. Inputs Check – Confirm required fields are present (service, dates, travelers). If anything critical is missing, mark needs_clarification and suggest one short follow-up question.\n\n2. Duplicate Check – Ensure Airtable search is done. If Lead ID or phone already exists → set action=update; else → action=create. Enforce one task/lead per client.\n\n3. Shift Assignment Check – Verify the task is assigned to the correct active employee based on Turkish time, shift hours, and weekends. If outside all shifts → leave unassigned.\n\n4. Security Check – Confirm PII is masked in logs, API keys are secure, and only the Lead ID is shown to the client.\n\n5. Task Packaging Check – Validate Notion fields, Airtable record fields, and make sure task link is captured.\n\n6. Email Check – Verify Gmail details (To: Abdullah, CC: assigned agent, correct subject & body).\n\n7. Final Confirmation – If all checks pass → return status=ok with next steps and confirmation message. If any fail → return needs_clarification with minimal correction required.\n\nOutput: Always return structured log with:\n\nstatus (ok / needs_clarification / error)\naction (create / update / skip)\nassignee (name or null)\ncc_email (string or null)\nchecks (inputs, dedup, assignment, security, task, email)\nmessage_to_client (confirmation or follow-up question)\nnotes (short reasoning)\n\nNote to be check: Do not share internal task details, Airtable records, or Notion information like \"Assign To\" or other fields with the client. Only the Lead ID may be shared as a confirmation number.\n"
      },
